help:subtopic.help:description:
A clock starts with base
      plus one increment, so first go includes increment. Measured wall time is deducted. Below -timemargin is a loss;
      otherwise negative becomes zero and increment is added. timemargin is milliseconds. st resets after each in-time move.

PGN/EPD append true by default;
      false truncates fresh output. Writes are mutex-protected but not schedule-reordered, so concurrency yields
      completion/write-lock order. Loaded stats force append despite false.

-testEnv, -strict,
      explicit affinity CPU list, startup-ms, ucinewgame-ms, ping-ms, and tbadjudicate filter. Re-specify on resume;
      tablebase filter otherwise returns to BOTH.
